      <p>The fish allergy point is the one most brands skip, and it is the one that applies to us directly. Both Dr Collagen shots are Japanese hydrolysed <a href="/pages/marine-collagen">marine collagen</a>, so neither is suitable if you are allergic to fish. It is not enough to say "hydrolysis removes the allergen" either. The 2020 study in the <em>Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology: In Practice</em> that found 21 of 101 fish-allergic patients sensitised to collagen also found that eight of them had no parvalbumin-specific IgE to some fish species, meaning a standard panel can return a result that misses the thing in the bottle. Fish collagen is now registered as an allergen in the WHO and IUIS database. A case report in <em>Allergology International</em> in 2016 describes anaphylaxis after someone ate hydrolysed fish collagen.</p>
      <p>Shellfish allergy is a separate protein and not the same question, but if you react to prawn or crab and have never been tested for fish, get tested before you start rather than after.</p>

