      <h2 id="see-a-doctor">When to see a doctor</h2>
      <p>Stop the supplement and seek medical help the same day if you develop any of the following after a dose: swelling of the lips, tongue or throat, difficulty breathing, widespread hives, or faintness. Those are features of an allergic reaction, and with a marine product the most likely trigger is the fish protein.</p>
      <p>Book an appointment, without urgency, if you get flank or back pain with blood in the urine, if persistent nausea or vomiting follows every dose, or if digestive symptoms have not settled after two weeks. Also see a doctor rather than a supplement if the problem you are treating is heavy hair shedding, severe joint pain, or sudden skin change. Those need a diagnosis first. <a href="/pages/how-long-does-collagen-take-to-work">Collagen works on a timescale of months</a>, which makes it a poor choice for anything that needs answering now.</p>

